The organisation knows its business context and the requirements of its interested parties, and it has defined what its information security management system (ISMS) covers.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs an ISMS, for example to meet NIS2 or to get an ISO/IEC 27001 certificate. A team that only needs the central controls for its products does not need it.

== How to implement

Describe the context of the organisation, the internal and external issues, and the interested parties and their requirements. Then define the scope of the ISMS: the organisational units, the locations, the services, and the information systems. Give a reason for each exclusion.

